---
source: crates/sshpick-cli/src/cli/test.rs
expression: "versionless(help::render(None, width, PLAIN))"
---
sshpick [version]

  ▌ sshpick [command] [query]... [options]

  Scripts and agents: ls, inspect and
  doctor take --json and change nothing.

  Commands:
    pick       Pick a host and ssh to it
               (default)
    ls | list  List the hosts that match a
               query
    inspect    Show where a host resolves
    doctor     Check the config, ssh and this
               terminal
    help       Show help for a command

  Global Options:
  -h,  --help             Output usage
                          information
       --no-color         Disable color
       --non-interactive  Never open the
                          picker;
                          connect only
                          when exactly
                          one host
                          matches
  -V,  --version          Output the
                          version number

  Environment:
  NO_COLOR        No color; bold, dim
                  and reverse video stay
                  on a terminal
  CLICOLOR_FORCE  Keep color when output
                  is not a terminal
  TERM            dumb: no color or
                  bold, and the picker
                  will not open

  Exit Status:
  0    Success; after a pick, ssh's own
       status
  1    No host matches
  2    Usage, config or ssh error; a
       failed doctor check; several
       matches where one is needed
  127  ssh could not be run
  130  Cancelled

  Examples:
  Open the picker filtered to hosts matching both words
    sshpick new consul

  Print the matching host names for a script
    sshpick list new consul | cut -f2

  Show where a host resolves
    sshpick inspect stg-consul1

  Learn more: https://github.com/PunGrumpy/sshpick#readme
